[[div class="page"]]



[[size 125%]]

When you can't walk, you write.

@@ @@

[[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]] We aren't getting through this. [[/span]] So those plans I had about [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]] asking Angel out on a date aren't [[/span]]going to work. Angel died two days ago. At least with the others, it took only a few days for them to die. It took Angel a few weeks. I saw his eyelids and nails fall out, [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]] then over the next few days,[[/span]] he said his skin was falling off. I didn't even believe him until [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]I saw the skin over his foot [[/span]] peel off in one layer. It grew back after a few [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]hours, but large [[/span]] chunks kept [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]falling off in entire pieces faster and faster. [[/span]] I thought it would at least be over in a few days, but he just kept recovering and it kept happening over and over again. At one point I even saw his face fucking fall off. [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]He didn't even have most of his nose when it came back.[[/span]] He spent so many hours vomiting and shitting blood, I don't even know if a human has that much [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]blood. I mean, whatever the fucking drink is probably keeps replacing his blood with new stuff.[[/span]] When I was a teen, I remember hearing of this Japanese man whose body couldn't heal from injuries. Of course, young me with unlimited internet access wanted to see pictures of it. I feel like teen me seeing those pictures for the first time. Only I see them 24/7, and I can't stop it.

[[/size]]

@@ @@

-----

@@ @@

[[size 125%]]

[[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]] A few days before Angel died,[[/span]] things started getting worse for me. I can't move at all below my chest, and weird bumps are forming on my skin. My hands are already deformed, [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]and I don't know what is happening.[[/span]] I can't feel my legs anymore. I had to crawl in here from outside to avoid a storm. [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]My hands are [[/span]] barely moving. [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]] I'm assuming Kellen and Zach are already dead, if not then they are assholes for choosing to not [[/span]] send help. We were too harsh with [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]] Zach. I mean, it definitely wasn't his fault. He drank it too,[[/span]] but of course we blamed him for it. We needed to [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]blame someone, and in doing so we sentenced him and Kellen to die alone. [[/span]] We are great people. 

@@ @@

I guess if I am going to die, [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]I might as well put down what I know. Even though the biggest question is [[/span]] why this happened. [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]] The story about this being a drink to help the workers is full of shit. We checked the [[/span]] town hal[[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]l, and the companies that "own" the factory just popped into existence one day. No records about the factory[[/span]] existing be[[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]fore 1921. They also never actually named any employees, just the letter "D" followed by a number.[[/span]] Something else [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]happened in here. Some experiment.[[/span]]

@@ @@

But it doesn't matter. Not anymore to me at least. I can't even feel my lower body anymore. I'm putting the journal in my backpack, so if anyone finds us [[span style="filter: blur(8px);"]]they can know what happened.[[/span]] 

@@ @@

I don't think we'll be found.



[[/size]]

[[>]]

Azrael.

