**Description:** SCP-7467-1 is a pair of bracelets made of [[span class="hoverlink"]][# Viellium][[span class="hoverlink-card"]][[span class="hoverlink-title"]]Viellium[[/span]][[span class="hoverlink-text" style="font-size:90%;"]]**Viellium** or //**Viátuva**// @@(@@[[size smaller]]Daevite:[[/size]] @@[@@[[[https://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/old-daevite-language|vi͡ɒtuʋa]]]@@]@@; meaning 'metal from [# Viálos]'@@)@@ is an alloy of bronze, orichalcum and beryllium made by the Daevite Empire. The highest grade of viellium had a pale golden color and was made with 36.5% beryllium, 50.6% bronze and 12.9% orichalcum.[[/span]][[span class="hoverlink-image" style="--src: url(https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Electrum_%28Oaxaca%2C_Mexico%29_%2816674495873%29.jpg/960px-Electrum_%28Oaxaca%2C_Mexico%29_%2816674495873%29.jpg)"]]-[[/span]][[/span]][[/span]] with inscriptions in ancient daevite. SCP-7467-1 dates to the Low Daevic period[[footnote]]Also known as Proto-Daevic period. Encompasses the beginning of Daevite Empire. From 15,000 BC to 9,000 BC.[[/footnote]], in the reign of the //Xeátxa// [[span class="daevite"]]//(eXátax)//[[/span]] dynasty at the northwest Beulaeva Covenant. The primary function of SCP-7467-1 is to control and command SCP-7467-A and SCP-7467-B entities, subduing them if necessary, by activating the SCP-7467-2 instances they carry. 



