+++ Interview with Director Káenti Xofiṭaiṭ — City of the Sun

+++ By: Researcher Qian Ling



-----



[[<]]

[[div class="mz-outbox"]]

[[div class="mz-innerbox"]]

[BEGIN LOG]



[Director Káenti and researcher Qian sit in the cafeteria. After waiting a while and having a brief chat, their food arrives.]



**Qian:** I hope you are having a good day, //Kharcist//. Thank you for accepting my invitation.



**Káenti:** Oh, please, you know you don't need to call me that. I'm not even //Kharcist//, we are family Qian. Just call me Grandma like everyone else.



**Qian:** Hehe, okay, okay. Grandma, when did you create //Kueše Átigná//?



**Káenti:** My boy, that's one of the many names the group has had. Let me tell you something. How old do you think I am?



**Qian:** Mhhhh… 80?



**Káenti:** Aw please, let's be serious this time.



**Qian:** Mhhh… At least 3,000 years, which on its own is quite a lot for a Daeva… With all due respect.



**Káenti:** Haha, don't worry. I'll give you a hint… I've seen an entire empire rise and fall an lived to tell it's story.



**Qian:** What—No. Are you saying?… 



**Káenti:** Mhm!



**Qian:** You are… Older than 10,000 years?…



**Káenti:** A little more, but I think if I keep going you'll die of a heart attack. I was one of the first Daevas to exist, Qian, or rather, I was part of the first generation of Daevas over 10,000 years ago.



**Qian:** But. How did you?…



**Káenti:** Thaumaturgy and technology[[footnote]]The original fragment refers to it as 'magic and alchemy'. For modern understanding, the words has been modified.[[/footnote]] my boy. My days should have ended a long time ago, but… My burden has kept me from accepting that end. To be honest, there's nothing left of what I ones was now, just a remnant. Sometimes I look out at the landscape and think about everything I've lived thru, all my children I've had to bury…



**Qian:** How many have—?



**Káenti:** This is the 54th group.



**Qian:** You… You saw all of them get older?…



**Káenti:** …Not many actually… There was always people that hates what you do…



**Qian:** Oh… I'm so sorry…



**Káenti:** …You don't have to… Many of them are already a blurry memory, which makes the pain feel less heavy.



**Qian:** Do they know?



**Káenti:** Yes. It seems like just yesterday when I told them. They wouldn't stop whining until they fell asleep.



**Qian:** …



**Káenti:** It's okay, my child. You don't have to feel bad for me. I chose this life.



**Qian:** …Why?



**Káenti:** Don't tell me you forgot what i taught you.



**Qian:** No. I'm very aware of that. But why? You're one of the first daevas and daevites in history… What did you lived that made you walk this path?



**Káenti:** Mhhh… When the sky still bled [[footnote]]A phrase from Daevite folklore used to begin, leyends, stories and tales; equivalent to our 'Once upon a time…'.[[/footnote]], a daevite emerged named //Nihiḳta Xeátxa//, as strong as her mother, //Ivurga Xeátxa//, and every bit the strategist her father, //Tahluz//, was. Born in //Viálos//, one of the ancient capital cities of a thriving empire in development.



Unfortunately, their happiness was interrupted by an unprecedented event. Her parents, the leaders of a young Daevite Empire, were… Found… Murdered in their chambers in the early hours of the sun. Servants, guards, leaders… Almost everyone in the house was murdered in cold blood…



**Qian:** Oh…



**Káenti:** …The poor girl, barely able to process the loss of her parents, rose to the position of matriarch. She immediately ordered a search for her parents' killer. However, no one was ever held responsible. Her pain became obsession, fueling deep resentment toward her people, whom she believed were against her.



Cold executions were carried out without mercy against anyone who contradicted the young matriarch. Under her blind gaze, she found only a light that illuminated her path, an energy emanating from her that altered reality in ways she desired.



**Qian:** She discovered thaumaturgy.



**Káenti:** A very primitive form. But it was enough for her to begin establishing centers of control over her people, or, as she called them, temples to a 'god' who had blessed her, //Haḳei//. She said she had found peace, promised she will bless with forgiveness, swear to lead her people to an utopia alongside their god… All nothing but a slow, silent, massacre.



For years, //Nihiḳta// tried to control her people's minds with cheap spells… Well, they were the best of the time, yet she still partially succeeded, leading most of her people to fall for her lie. At the peak of her delusion, she named her caregiver, the woman who had cared for her since childhood and the only person she trusted, the 'first priestess' tasked with leading the Daevites to the next stage with the help of that god.



**Qian:** Were you her caregiver?!



**Káenti:** …Yes.



**Qian:** So that's how you learned thaumaturgy…



**Káenti:** I was always very close to //Nihiḳta//. After all, I was the one she spent the most time with, and after her parents' death I had to take complete care of her. The position of—



**Qian:** What was //Nihiḳta// like? You know, before… 



**Káenti:** She was a stubborn girl, full of conviction. You could say she was mulish, but once you showed her she was wrong, she'd immediately learn so she wouldn't make the same mistake. She really enjoyed hunting and even participated in one with her father.



**Qian:** Oh, it must have been… It must have been hard to see her change so much…



**Káenti:** …Ahem… The position of first priestess was nothing more than being the public face while concealing the matriarch's real intentions. I… I was nothing more than a privileged puppet repeating what I was told… Augh…



**Qian:** It's okay if you don't share that part. I don't want to force you to remember something like that.



**Káenti:** No. It's just… Don't worry. It's what I deserve for having lived the life I did. I just… I still have trouble accepting it.



**Qian:** I understand… Would you like something, some water?



**Káenti:** Thank you… Hah… You might wonder what kind of things I had to hide. Well, several of those things now lie beneath your feet. One of them lies deep within the Temple of //Haḳei//, the very temple your ancestors came to investigate many years ago.



**Qian:** Oh… Hm… Grandma?



**Káenti:** Mh?



**Qian:** Can I… Know what it is?…



**Káenti:** …Mh… I suppose… Sooner or later I'll have to do it… //Nihiḳta//, in her... Madness, she created a series of earrings that she distributed among her people as religious garments, and thanks to the slight control she exerted over them, she managed to get almost everyone to wear them. First it was the earrings, then the tattoos in the name of //Haḳei//, then the ceremonial necklaces… Little by little, she was preparing her new slaves, and no one but me knew it…



I never understood how she managed to create the ritual, but once the entire village wore the garments, it began. While everyone prayed in unison, //Nihiḳta// put on special bracelets and calmly recited that… Poem…





