-----



[[<]]

[[div class="blockquote" style="background: #96182b; color: #fff; padding-bottom: 0.25em"]]

{{= [BEGIN LOG] =}}

[[/div]]

[Researcher Guangli and director Xofiṭaiṭ arrive at the café, and after a friendly chat over food, they become more familiar with each other.]



**Guangli:** Again. thank you very much, Director, for giving me the opportunity to conduct this research.



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** It's nothing, really. If there's one thing I enjoy more than seeing you happy, it's seeing you grow up. It was… Time to leave the weight of the past behind and establish a better future for you. I suppose this will help the relations with the Foundation.



**Guangli:** Yep. Although, before I send it, would you like me to omit or change any part of it? It's… your story, after all, and I wouldn't want to tarnish your—



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Don't worry, it's better to leave the story as it is. I spent a long time hiding it. You have the right to know the truth behind this place and… Behind me. What kind of leader would I be if I hid my past from you?



**Guangli:** Hm, I suppose so… Even so, you're still the best grandma!



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Aww, please, my child…



**Guangli:** Hehe~. AH! Just one more question, Director.



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Mh? About what, dear?



**Guangli:** It's about the //Henma//… Was it all made up by //Nihiḳta//?



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Well… Although I still got along 'well' with //Nihiḳta// at that time, she was always very secretive about the reasons behind her actions. When she started talking about //Henma//, she never said more than what I intuited. Although she seemed convinced that //Haḳei// existed… I always suspected that it was more than just her delusion, but that was all, just suspicions.



**Guangli:** And what became of //Henma// after her death?



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Mh, what could you expect from a bunch of power-hungry leaders. They saw its potential and simply renamed it and added things… They saw the power that lay behind a god to their people.



**Guangli:** Ah… That makes sense.



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** But still…



**Guangli:** Mh?



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** We… We never practised thaumaturgy until much later, we didn't even know what it was… I don't understand how //Nihiḳta// managed to do that on her own…



**Guangli:** Perhaps someone helped her?



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** No, she never spoke to anyone else privately. She kept her paranoia, even though she tried to hid it. And as I said, no one else even knew that thaumaturgy was a thing.



**Guangli:** …



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Mh…



**Guangli:** …Do you think that…



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** I gain nothing by concluding an answer. After all, it's something that already happened… But I suppose you already have a topic for your next investigation, little one.



**Guangli:** Oh, I wish it were the only one. But I'll have to postpone it, it's a very different topic from my main department and…



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** I understand, I understand. I was just suggesting, don't worry about it.



**Guangli:** AH! THE TIME! I am very sorry to have to leave like this, Director.



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Oh, please. I had a lovely time with you. Go on, take care and have a lovely day, darling.



**Guangli:** Goodbye, Grandma!



**Xofiṭaiṭ:** Ehm... The...



**Guangli:** MY CAMERA!

[[div class="blockquote" style="background: #96182b; color: #fff; padding-bottom: 0.25em"]]

{{= [END LOG] =}}

